    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d400">

                <pb facs="0619" n="517" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg517"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.79640/102</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Lindsay</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                        </hi><anchor n="8" xml:id="d400-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 328</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-11-27">November 27,
                        1935</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to refer to your note of
                    the 12th November and to inform you that the United Kingdom Air Mission, which
                    will probably arrive in Washington on December 2nd, desires to discuss with the
                    United States Inter-departmental Committee on Civil International Aviation
                    proposals for the joint operation, under government auspices, of trans-Atlantic
                    air services between the United Kingdom and the United States of America by a
                    company nominated by His Majesty’s Governments concerned and an American
                    company, with particular reference to a route passing through the Irish Free
                    State, Newfoundland and Montreal.</p>
                <p>The discussions would include the following subjects:— <list>
                        <label>(1)</label>
                        <item>Postal arrangements;</item>
                        <label>(2)</label>
                        <item>Arrangements for terminal air ports and landing rights;</item>
                        <label>(3)</label>
                        <item>Methods of operation;</item>
                        <label>(4)</label>
                        <item>Frequency of services;</item>
                        <label>(5)</label>
                        <item>Ground organisation;</item>
                        <label>(6)</label>
                        <item>Programme of experimental and development work.</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>R. C. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lindsay</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d400-f1" n="8" type="source" xml:id="d400-f1-content">
                <p>Notes similar in substance were received from the Canadian Chargé, November 29,
                    1935, and the Irish Minister, November 27, 1935.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
